  "result": "Perfect! All 212 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary: Payment Terms Feature\n\n### New/Updated: `src/invoices.js`\n\n**`calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`** \u2014 Helper function\n- Calculates invoice due dates based on payment terms\n- NET14: Issue date + 14 days\n- NET30: Issue date + 30 days (default)\n- EOM: Last day of the issue month (handles leap years and month boundaries)\n\n**Updated `createInvoice()`**\n- Now accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Validates terms against: 'NET14', 'NET30', 'EOM'\n- Returns error `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the created invoice\n\n**Updated `issueInvoice()`, `addLine()`, `removeLine()`**\n- Now preserve `terms` and `dueDate` when modifying invoices\n\n### Updated: `src/errors.js`\n\nAdded new error code:\n- `TERMS_INVALID` \u2014 Payment terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n### Tests: `test/terms.test.js`\n\nComprehensive test suite with 34 tests covering:\n- Default and explicit term selection\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Error handling (invalid terms, case sensitivity, null/undefined)\n- Due date calculations for:\n  - All month types (28/29/30/31 days)\n  - Leap years and non-leap years\n  - Month and year boundaries\n- Term preservation through invoice operations (issue, addLine, removeLine)\n- Edge cases and validation order\n\n**Test Results:** All 212 tests pass \u2713",
